{{> head}}
{{> nav}}
<main id="main">

  <section class="section hero scheme-dark case-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="container hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>About</p>
          <h1 class="h1" id="about-title" data-split>Who is <span class="mark">behind<svg class="mark__svg" viewBox="0 0 240 24" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-draw><path d="M4 15 C 46 8, 92 19, 136 12 S 210 7, 236 13"/></svg></span> Libre Studio?</h1>
          <p class="text-lg" data-reveal>Libre Studio is a remote product design studio for startups, founded by Başak Feyzioğlu and based in Istanbul. We design web and mobile products end to end, from user research to a prototype developers can build, with AI-assisted workflows and a human in the loop.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="facts" data-reveal>
        <div><dt>Founder</dt><dd>Başak Feyzioğlu</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Istanbul, working worldwide</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Designing since</dt><dd>2020</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Clients</dt><dd>Startups, mainly in the UK and US</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="founder-title" data-split>Who is Başak Feyzioğlu?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p>Başak Feyzioğlu founded Libre Studio. She is a product designer who has designed web and mobile products since 2020, for more than 10 clients in more than 10 countries.</p>
          <p>She came to design from law. She studied law at Koç University in Istanbul, then worked in M&amp;A and as an attorney until 2019. In 2020 she joined Pensa Systems as a business data analyst, preparing data for a computer-vision AI used in retail. The same year she co-authored <em>Data Protection Laws and Regulations in Turkey</em> for ICLG, comparing Turkish law with GDPR. That was her first work in AI, and her first published writing on data rights.</p>
          <p>She taught herself design through courses and real projects: a diploma from the UX Design Institute, graphic design training from CalArts, and generative AI certificates from Vanderbilt University. You can find her on <a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/basakfeyzioglu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="clients-title" data-split>What have we worked on?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p>Mostly startups in the UK and the US: AI-native consumer apps, B2B SaaS, dashboards and websites. Başak spent a year with the C-level team of a logistics SaaS company, designing three web products.</p>
          <p>Recent work includes <a class="text-link" href="/work/lula/">Lula</a>, an AI bedtime-story app, and <a class="text-link" href="/work/mona-ai/">MONA AI</a>, a photo and video studio app. Both are on the App Store. Earlier projects include Nyuk.in, a fintech app, and Whiteglasses, a sentiment-analysis dashboard.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-dark" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="how-title" data-split>How does Libre Studio work?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p>We are a small, senior studio. Başak leads every project and brings in senior freelance designers from our network when a project needs more hands. We are fully remote, based in Istanbul (GMT+3), and work with teams worldwide.</p>
          <p>AI is part of every step: research synthesis, iterations, documentation and handoff. We work in Figma, Claude Code and Cursor, and we build our own Claude Code skills for audits and reviews. A designer reviews every output and makes every call. AI does the legwork; the decisions stay human. More on that in <a class="text-link" href="/ai-design/">how we design with AI</a>.</p>
          <p>We work with high agency. We ask a lot of questions before we design, we push back when a brief points at the wrong problem, and we own the result through to handoff. Our work covers UI, UX and product design, <a class="text-link" href="/design-engineering/">design engineering</a>, <a class="text-link" href="/motion-design/">motion design</a> and <a class="text-link" href="/design-systems/">atomic design systems</a>, so the product, the marketing and the motion grow from one system.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-coral" aria-labelledby="beliefs-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="beliefs-title" data-split>What do we believe?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Users are tired of AI slop.</strong> We use AI everywhere except where they can see it.</li>
            <li><strong>Human in the loop, always.</strong> AI never ships work alone.</li>
            <li><strong>Design with intent.</strong> Every decision ties to a user problem and a business outcome. Pretty is not a deliverable.</li>
            <li><strong>Built for handoff.</strong> Tokens, components and clear names, so developers build without translating.</li>
            <li><strong>No black box.</strong> You see our process, our files and the reasons behind each decision.</li>
            <li><strong>The line keeps moving.</strong> Tools and user expectations change every month, so we keep learning in public.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-royal" aria-labelledby="about-cta-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <h2 class="h2" id="about-cta-title" data-split>Want to work with us?</h2>
        <p class="text-lg" data-reveal>Tell us what you are building. If you are a senior designer who likes owning your work, we would like to hear from you too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions actions--center" data-reveal>
        <a class="btn btn--lime" href="{{calendar}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="btn__label"><span data-text="Book a Call">Book a Call</span></span></a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost-dark" href="/careers/"><span class="btn__label"><span data-text="See careers">See careers</span></span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{> work-next}}
